    "summary": "- Period boundaries for monthly and yearly plans are computed from the anchor (StartedAt, or TrialEnd for trials) as `anchor + n months/years`, clamped to the month's last day. The anchor never drifts, and each period ends where the next starts.\n- `RenewDue` catches up every missed period in order, with one invoice per period, and the boundaries don't depend on when the job runs.\n- New tests cover Jan 31 and Feb 29 anchors, a trial ending on a month end, time-of-day preservation, a late run, and multi-period catch-up. `go build ./...`, `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` all pass.",
